"""H2-4 PPU and bus allocation (follow-on ``fo_h2_4_ppu_bus``, trigger ``T_H2_4_PPU_BUS``, owner addendum A7).

H2 hardware design / preliminary-sizing lane for the common electrical supplies PS-C of the H-1 test article and the
flight PPU of the A5 proposal reference architecture. It is NOT an architecture-selection lane (A7 ``h2_scope``): it
never predicts thrust, efficiency, discharge current or plasma state, never selects hall_only / rf_hall / ecr_hall and
never uses a Hall transport closure (the credible set is empty), abep_sim/plasma_devices.py (superseded 0-D Hall) or a
withdrawn v1.2-v1.6 number. Every number below is a requirement, an A5 allocation, a PROPOSED sub-allocation of this
lane, a published analog (labelled with device, source and evidence class), an engineering derivation (P = V I,
P_bus = P_load / eta, I_bus = P_bus / V_bus) or TBD / PENDING with what it requires.

What it does (deterministic, standard library + the read-only boundary module ``abep_sim.arch_boundary``):
  * refuses to run if a pinned input is missing or its sha256 differs (decision files A5/A6/A7, the G0 verification,
    verified repository deliverables); mutable governance files are never pinned;
  * builds the design-parameter table H24-nn, the per-component load list (ALLOCATION or PARAMETER, voltage/current
    ranges), the STEADY / STARTUP / PEAK bus profiles, the converter-efficiency parameters, the margin table, the
    discharge allocation (the residual of the A5 P_bus allocation, never a transport result), the reserved pre-ionizer
    slot headroom as a function of the unknown discharge share, the PPU architecture options, the grounding scheme and
    the H-1 ground-supply vs flight-PPU reconstruction rule for P_bus;
  * calls ``bus_power_ledger`` with the inputs that exist and records its refusal (nothing is defaulted);
  * writes ``h2_4_ppu_bus_v1.json`` and the companion ``H2_4_PPU_BUS.md`` (generated from the JSON).

Parallel lanes (H2-1/2/3/5/6/7, the A6 pre-ionizer ICD, Xe ledger, Phase-1 framework, M16 matrix) are referenced by path
as PENDING only; nothing here reads them. ``--pending-status`` reports lazily whether their directories exist yet; it
never changes the JSON.

    python docs/hardware/h2/h2_4_ppu_bus/build_h2_4_ppu_bus.py                    # (re)write the outputs
    python docs/hardware/h2/h2_4_ppu_bus/build_h2_4_ppu_bus.py --check            # byte-for-byte check (exit 1 on drift)
    python docs/hardware/h2/h2_4_ppu_bus/build_h2_4_ppu_bus.py --pending-status   # lazy presence report of PENDING lanes
"""
